\subsection{<<CMD_215>>: \texlive Version Differences}<<CMD_260>>

\paragraph{Overview} 

We found significant differences in the compilation results of different versions of \texlive.
Similar to the inter-engine comparison, the most common type of inconsistencies were differences in text spacing, which were usually relatively minor:
such differences were mostly small shifts in the position of characters on a page, and did not affect the information conveyed in the document.
However, more ``major'' differences affecting the content of the document were still prevalent.
